    "TaskOperationService": {
      "action": "modify",
      "docs": "Pre-existing primary port for track task mutations; transition_task's success type becomes TaskTransitionOutcome so an admission refusal travels as typed data. Type-design: no admission-specific method is added — the judgment stays inside transition_task's implementation; the other three operations and the error type are untouched. transition_task channels: structured lane = Ok(TaskTransitionOutcome::Rejected(AdmissionRejectionOutput)) — judged refusals, data for callers; Err lane = TaskOperationError::TransitionFailed(String) — unjudgeable states as terminal diagnostics. Asymmetry with the gate path's BatchPlanViolationOutput is intentional: track-ops errors are rendered immediately as string CommandOutcome by the composition root (accepted interim boundary), so a structured error variant would have no consumer; TaskOperationError stays baseline-shaped and undeclared here. CN-10.",
