    "BatchPlanCheckInteractor": {
      "action": "add",
      "docs": "Implements BatchPlanCheckService: resolves the track context with READ semantics through the pre-existing resolve service, reads the batch plan, the planned tasks and the scope config through its three injected ports, and delegates to check_batch_plan, then maps the domain verdict into this crate's output DTO. Type-design: resolution is absorbed here rather than performed by the adapter beforehand, so one request drives one interactor; it reuses the shared resolve service instead of a second mechanism. The domain-to-DTO mapping lives here so the domain verdict stops at this layer. Holds no ceiling arithmetic of its own, and an absent batch plan is mapped to an error rather than a pass — the opposite of the pre-review task-contract gate's absent-artifact tolerance. IN-06, IN-07, AC-05, AC-06, AC-07, AC-08, CN-09.",
