    "TaskTransitionOutcome": {
      "action": "add",
      "docs": "Result of transition_task: the transition happened, or it was refused with the typed reason. Type-design: an admission refusal is a legitimate result rather than an exceptional condition, so it travels as data and keeps its scope, contribution, ceiling and batch payloads intact — the same outcome-as-data shape the Phase 3 gate path uses, instead of collapsing to a rendered string in the error channel. The refusal is carried as this crate's own output DTO, so no domain value object reaches the adapter. This also leaves TaskOperationError's declared shape identical to its baseline. Role Dto in usecase (R1 △, justification): it is the output carrier of the pre-existing TaskOperationOutput DTO in this same module, crossing the usecase-to-driver boundary; it is not identified by value equality, so ValueObject would be the wrong classification. IN-09, IN-10, AC-10, AC-12.",
